{
  "$schema": "https://ui.shadcn.com/schema/registry.json",
  "name": "rud",
  "homepage": "https://github.com/ofirrubin/react-dashboard-builder",
  "items": [
    {
      "name": "dashboard",
      "type": "registry:block",
      "title": "Dashboard",
      "description": "A draggable, resizable widget grid built on your own shadcn primitives and theme tokens.",
      "author": "Ofir Rubin",
      "categories": [
        "dashboard",
        "layout"
      ],
      "dependencies": [
        "rud-dashboard@^0.2.0",
        "lucide-react"
      ],
      "registryDependencies": [
        "badge",
        "button",
        "card",
        "empty",
        "field",
        "popover",
        "separator",
        "switch",
        "toggle-group",
        "tooltip"
      ],
      "files": [
        {
          "path": "registry/rud/dashboard/dashboard.tsx",
          "type": "registry:component",
          "target": "@components/dashboard/dashboard.tsx"
        },
        {
          "path": "registry/rud/dashboard/dashboard-item.tsx",
          "type": "registry:component",
          "target": "@components/dashboard/dashboard-item.tsx"
        },
        {
          "path": "registry/rud/dashboard/dashboard-toolbar.tsx",
          "type": "registry:component",
          "target": "@components/dashboard/dashboard-toolbar.tsx"
        },
        {
          "path": "registry/rud/dashboard/use-dashboard.ts",
          "type": "registry:hook",
          "target": "@components/dashboard/use-dashboard.ts"
        }
      ],
      "docs": "Render it with a widget catalog:\n\n  const widgets = {\n    revenue: {\n      title: \"Revenue\",\n      defaultSize: { w: 3, h: 3 },\n      render: () => <RevenueCard />,\n    },\n  }\n\n  <Dashboard widgets={widgets} defaultLayout={layout} onLayoutChange={save} />\n\nThe layout is plain JSON \u2014 persist it wherever you like. Nothing here ships CSS or a Tailwind config; every colour and radius comes from your existing theme tokens."
    },
    {
      "name": "dashboard-widgets",
      "type": "registry:block",
      "title": "Dashboard widgets",
      "description": "Ready-made widget bodies: stat, progress, chart, and Typeset-styled prose.",
      "author": "Ofir Rubin",
      "categories": [
        "dashboard"
      ],
      "dependencies": [
        "lucide-react"
      ],
      "registryDependencies": [
        "badge",
        "chart",
        "progress",
        "@rud/dashboard-theme"
      ],
      "files": [
        {
          "path": "registry/rud/widgets/stat-widget.tsx",
          "type": "registry:component",
          "target": "@components/dashboard/widgets/stat-widget.tsx"
        },
        {
          "path": "registry/rud/widgets/progress-widget.tsx",
          "type": "registry:component",
          "target": "@components/dashboard/widgets/progress-widget.tsx"
        },
        {
          "path": "registry/rud/widgets/chart-widget.tsx",
          "type": "registry:component",
          "target": "@components/dashboard/widgets/chart-widget.tsx"
        },
        {
          "path": "registry/rud/widgets/notes-widget.tsx",
          "type": "registry:component",
          "target": "@components/dashboard/widgets/notes-widget.tsx"
        }
      ],
      "docs": "These are ordinary components \u2014 edit or delete them freely. They take data as props and hold no state, so they work outside the dashboard too."
    },
    {
      "name": "dashboard-theme",
      "type": "registry:theme",
      "title": "Dashboard theme",
      "description": "Optional polish: layered depth, drag feedback, and a compact prose rhythm for widget text.",
      "author": "Ofir Rubin",
      "categories": [
        "dashboard",
        "theme"
      ],
      "cssVars": {
        "theme": {
          "--dashboard-lift": "0 1px 2px -1px oklch(0% 0 0 / 0.08), 0 4px 12px -4px oklch(0% 0 0 / 0.10)",
          "--dashboard-lift-hover": "0 2px 4px -2px oklch(0% 0 0 / 0.10), 0 12px 28px -8px oklch(0% 0 0 / 0.16)",
          "--dashboard-lift-active": "0 8px 20px -4px oklch(0% 0 0 / 0.18), 0 24px 48px -12px oklch(0% 0 0 / 0.22)"
        }
      },
      "css": {
        "@layer components": {
          "[data-slot=dashboard-item]": {
            "box-shadow": "var(--dashboard-lift)",
            "transition-property": "box-shadow, transform, opacity",
            "transition-duration": "180ms",
            "transition-timing-function": "cubic-bezier(0.2, 0, 0, 1)",
            "&:hover": {
              "box-shadow": "var(--dashboard-lift-hover)"
            },
            "&[data-editing]:hover": {
              "transform": "translateY(-1px)"
            },
            "&[data-active]": {
              "box-shadow": "var(--dashboard-lift-active)"
            }
          },
          "[data-slot=dashboard-item] > [data-slot=card-header]": {
            "background-image": "linear-gradient(to bottom, color-mix(in oklab, var(--muted) 45%, transparent), transparent)"
          },
          "[data-slot=dashboard-canvas][data-editing]": {
            "box-shadow": "inset 0 0 0 1px color-mix(in oklab, var(--primary) 18%, transparent)"
          },
          "[data-slot=dashboard-preview]": {
            "animation": "dashboard-preview-pulse 1.4s ease-in-out infinite"
          }
        },
        "@keyframes dashboard-preview-pulse": {
          "0%, 100%": {
            "opacity": "1"
          },
          "50%": {
            "opacity": "0.62"
          }
        },
        "@media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)": {
          "[data-slot=dashboard-item], [data-slot=dashboard-preview]": {
            "transition": "none",
            "animation": "none"
          },
          "[data-slot=dashboard-widget-bar] *": {
            "animation": "none",
            "transition": "none"
          }
        },
        ".typeset-widget": {
          "--typeset-size": "0.8125rem",
          "--typeset-leading": "1.6",
          "--typeset-flow": "0.85em"
        },
        "@layer base": {
          ":where(.typeset)": {
            "font-size": "var(--typeset-size, 0.875rem)",
            "line-height": "var(--typeset-leading, 1.7)",
            "color": "var(--foreground)"
          },
          ":where(.typeset) :where(h1, h2, h3, h4, h5, h6)": {
            "font-weight": "600",
            "line-height": "1.25",
            "margin-block-start": "var(--typeset-flow, 1em)",
            "text-wrap": "balance"
          },
          ":where(.typeset) :where(h1)": {
            "font-size": "1.5em"
          },
          ":where(.typeset) :where(h2)": {
            "font-size": "1.25em"
          },
          ":where(.typeset) :where(h3)": {
            "font-size": "1.0625em"
          },
          ":where(.typeset) :where(p, ul, ol, blockquote, pre, table, hr)": {
            "margin-block-start": "var(--typeset-flow, 1em)"
          },
          ":where(.typeset) > :where(:first-child)": {
            "margin-block-start": "0"
          },
          ":where(.typeset) :where(ul, ol)": {
            "padding-inline-start": "1.5em"
          },
          ":where(.typeset) :where(ul)": {
            "list-style-type": "disc"
          },
          ":where(.typeset) :where(ol)": {
            "list-style-type": "decimal"
          },
          ":where(.typeset) :where(li)": {
            "margin-block-start": "calc(var(--typeset-flow, 1em) * 0.35)"
          },
          ":where(.typeset) :where(a)": {
            "color": "var(--primary)",
            "text-decoration-line": "underline",
            "text-underline-offset": "2px"
          },
          ":where(.typeset) :where(strong)": {
            "font-weight": "600"
          },
          ":where(.typeset) :where(code)": {
            "font-family": "var(--font-mono, ui-monospace, monospace)",
            "font-size": "0.875em",
            "background-color": "var(--muted)",
            "border-radius": "calc(var(--radius) - 4px)",
            "padding": "0.15em 0.35em"
          },
          ":where(.typeset) :where(pre)": {
            "font-family": "var(--font-mono, ui-monospace, monospace)",
            "font-size": "0.8125em",
            "background-color": "var(--muted)",
            "border-radius": "var(--radius)",
            "padding": "0.75em 1em",
            "overflow-x": "auto"
          },
          ":where(.typeset) :where(pre) :where(code)": {
            "background-color": "transparent",
            "padding": "0"
          },
          ":where(.typeset) :where(blockquote)": {
            "border-inline-start": "2px solid var(--border)",
            "padding-inline-start": "1em",
            "color": "var(--muted-foreground)"
          },
          ":where(.typeset) :where(hr)": {
            "border-color": "var(--border)"
          },
          ":where(.typeset) :where(.not-typeset, [data-not-typeset]) :where(*)": {
            "margin-block-start": "revert",
            "font-size": "revert",
            "line-height": "revert"
          },
          ":where(.typeset) :where(p, li, blockquote)": {
            "text-wrap": "pretty"
          }
        },
        "@keyframes dashboard-grow-y": {
          "from": {
            "transform": "scaleY(0.04)",
            "opacity": "0.4"
          },
          "to": {
            "transform": "scaleY(1)",
            "opacity": "1"
          }
        },
        "@keyframes dashboard-fill-x": {
          "from": {
            "transform": "scaleX(0)"
          },
          "to": {
            "transform": "scaleX(1)"
          }
        }
      },
      "files": [],
      "docs": "Entirely optional \u2014 the dashboard already looks correct on your theme tokens without it.\n\nThis adds three things:\n  1. Layered depth and drag feedback, hooked onto [data-slot=dashboard-*] so no component file changes.\n  2. A compact `.typeset-widget` rhythm preset for prose widgets.\n  3. A small `.typeset` prose layer, in case you have not installed shadcn Typeset.\n\nAlready using Typeset? Its own CSS covers item 3; keep this item only for the depth and the `.typeset-widget` preset, and delete the `:where(.typeset)` rules from your CSS file.\n\nAll shadows use `oklch`/`color-mix` against your existing tokens, so light and dark both follow the host theme automatically."
    },
    {
      "name": "dashboard-demo",
      "type": "registry:block",
      "title": "Dashboard demo",
      "description": "A complete, working dashboard page: six widgets, localStorage persistence, and a reset control.",
      "author": "Ofir Rubin",
      "categories": [
        "dashboard",
        "example"
      ],
      "registryDependencies": [
        "button",
        "@rud/dashboard",
        "@rud/dashboard-widgets"
      ],
      "files": [
        {
          "path": "registry/rud/example/dashboard-demo.tsx",
          "type": "registry:component",
          "target": "@components/dashboard-demo.tsx"
        }
      ],
      "docs": "Drop it straight into a route:\n\n  import { DashboardDemo } from \"@/components/dashboard-demo\"\n\n  export default function Page() {\n    return <div className=\"p-6\"><DashboardDemo /></div>\n  }\n\nIt is meant to be read and then edited \u2014 the widget catalog at the top of the file is the only part you need to change to make it yours."
    }
  ]
}
